{text}

{evidence}" — the subject's text then its evidence, no labels. Sentences (94-100): split at . ; : followed by whitespace and an opening character, or at a blank line, keeping units longer than 12 characters. `pick_with` (188-237): one `choice` "which" whose options are S1..Sn (the units' own text) plus NONE, asked "Which {unit} of the author's text disagrees with the captured evidence? A disagreeing {unit} asserts something the captured evidence, or the author's own figures elsewhere in the text, show to be otherwise"; with classify, one further `choice` per unit over KIND (CURRENT / PROPOSED / ARGUMENT, 180-185). Score: with classify, the sum over units of P(unit) x P(CURRENT of unit); without, 1 - P(NONE). VARIANTS (314-326): `pick_cls` = sentences, classify on, NONE = "No sentence disagrees with the evidence. " + NOT_A_DISAGREEMENT; `pick_clause` = unit "clause", classify off, NONE = "No clause disagrees with the evidence. " + NOT_A_DISAGREEMENT. Clauses (248-257) cut at every `,` `;` `:` ` —` ` –` followed by whitespace — no bracket or code-span awareness — keeping units longer than 12 characters. NOT_A_DISAGREEMENT (gate_jev.py:33-37): "Also false when: the evidence merely fails to establish the text; the capture does not touch what the text is about; the text says less than the evidence shows; the text describes what a design PROPOSES to build, which evidence captured beforehand cannot contradict; or the reader is simply uncertain. Insufficiency is not disagreement."

